id: pm-jau2
title: Clarify reconciliation evidence limits in merge-safety documentation
description: The README overstates lossless-merge guarantees and advertises raw history repair. Bring it into alignment with the CI workflow distinction between durable tracker health and evidence that every source value survived a merge. This follow-up is deferred from dependency PR 142.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,docs,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-22T19:46:00.288Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T07:45:41.540Z"
author: claude-opus-20260722
acceptance_criteria: Document current audited reconciliation semantics; remove unconditional no-data-loss and raw-repair guidance; require independent source and receipt verification; keep health and lossless-merge claims separate.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T07:38:58.805Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up discovered while repairing PR 142: the current README generalizes a successful historical merge experiment into an unconditional no-data-loss claim, describes reconciliation as re-greening hashes, and still advertises raw history repair. The CI workflow correctly distinguishes strict health from lossless-merge evidence. Review the README against current audited reconciliation semantics and require source/evidence verification rather than treating green health as proof of losslessness. Deferred from the dependency repair; no history rewrite or repair was performed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-22T19:46:00.661Z",claude-opus-20260722,Fan-out from canary unbraind/pm-beads#42. README Multi-agent merge safety section closing recommendation migrated to the pm merge reconcile dry-run->apply->verify workflow; links upstream docs/MERGE_SAFETY.md; keeps history-repair --all as a lower-level primitive.
files[1]{path,scope}:
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project
docs[1]{path,scope}:
  README.md,project
body: ""
